[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Not for Jazz]
[00:00.54]What happened to the clavichord? |
[00:11.96]We have an old musical instrument. |
[00:15.82]It is called a clavichord. |
[00:18.58]It was made in Germany in 1681. |
[00:23.16]Our clavichord is kept in the living room. |
[00:26.78]It has belonged to our family for a long time. |
[00:31.18]The instrument was bought by my grandfather many years ago. |
[00:36.02]Recently it was damaged by a visitor. |
[00:39.43]She tried to play jazz on it! |
[00:42.62]She struck the keys too hard and two of the strings were broken. |
[00:47.96]My father was shocked. |
[00:50.88]Now we are not allowed to touch it. |
[00:54.08]It is being repaired by a friend of my father's. |